"nLaunch":{"x":-500,"y":1504,"w":420,"fill":"orange","size":"m","text":"Launch animation (shown slowed down here as a 7 s loop)\n\nIn the app it runs once on a cold start and takes about 1 second; a tap skips it.\n\n1. Still launch screen (iOS shows it instantly): night sky, stars, crescent moon, the sun asleep and half under the night sea. No text.\n2. Sunrise, 0 to 0.5 s: the sky warms from night to dawn, the stars fade, the dunes light up, the sun rises and its rays unfold.\n3. Good morning, 0.5 to 0.65 s: the sun opens its eyes for a moment.\n4. Settle, 0.65 to 1 s: the sun glides and shrinks into its place on Today's arc while Home fades in underneath.\n\nReduce Motion: a 0.3 s cross-fade from the night frame to Home. Returning from the background: no animation."},
"nYearPhotos":{"x":5510,"y":4192,"w":420,"fill":"orange","size":"m","text":"Photos card: which six photos\n\nThe card favours the photos you keep coming back to.\n\n1. Each photo quietly counts how often it was opened in the photo viewer (at least 1 second on screen; scrolling past a thumbnail doesn't count). Opening it again within the same hour counts once.\n2. The card picks the six most returned-to photos of the year. Ties go to the more recent one.\n3. If fewer than six have been opened, the rest are filled with the most recent photos.\n4. Long-press a tile in the preview to swap it; a photo you swap in stays for that year.\n\nThe count is a small number stored with the session, and synced with iCloud only when sync is on. It's never shown anywhere, and deleting the photo deletes it too."},
